Research Session 003 · July 12, 2026
Purpose: Audit ChatGPT Entry 001 against Session 001 data · Apply QC flags to existing records · Resolve schema conflicts · Produce canonical working standards · Move the project forward

PART I — HONEST AUDIT OF CHATGPT ENTRY 001
What it does well
The methodological layer is genuinely strong. The Three-Map Rule, the QC flag system, the connection-type taxonomy, and the five hypotheses are all additions that improve the project. They formalize things that were implicit in Session 001 but never written down as rules.

The best single contribution is this line from QC-002:

Each major artifact family should eventually receive its own record.

That's correct and Session 001 violated it in several places.

What it does not do
The ChatGPT entry is entirely methodological. It produced zero new data records. It identified problems but did not fix any of them in the existing dataset. It recommended schemas but did not apply them to the records already on file.

That is not a criticism — methodology first is defensible — but it means the reconciliation work still needs to happen, and that is what this session does.

