PART V — WHAT CHATGPT ENTRY 001 MISSED
Being honest about the gaps:

1. No new data records were produced. The entry is 100% methodological. That is a legitimate first pass but means the data corpus did not grow. Session 001 has 68 records. Session 002/Entry 001 has zero new records. The ratio needs to rebalance.

2. The QC flags were not applied back to specific Session 001 records. The flags were written generically. This reconciliation document is the first time QC-001 through QC-006 have been applied to actual named records (GREY-002, SRP-005, etc.).

3. The Euler hollow Earth problem (HE-002) was not addressed. It was flagged in Session 001 as a secondary-source-only attribution. ChatGPT Entry 001 did not resolve it or add to it. It remains an open agent task.

4. The agent task queue from Session 001 was not touched. 12 specific tasks were queued. None were addressed in the methodology entry.

5. The map schema is excellent but has no populated examples. MAP-CHAIN-001 (Terra Australis) was correctly identified as the first controlled study, but no specific map records were created using the new schema.

